							<div align="center"><font color="#0000ff"><b>Necromancer Epic</b></font><br /> </div> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody><tr><td class="ContentBoxBody">Symbol of the Apprentice</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Kazen Facae at location 340, -1600 in Lake Rathetear and then say the following words: **The Head of Sir Edwin Motte - Dropped by Sir Edwin Motte who can be best found at the Inn at the East Freeport Docks. ***Note: Edwin is a level 33 Paly and is part of a rotation with Tumpy, Groflah, and a barbarian in leather at the Inn. Just kill these guys if they are there and wait for Edwin to spawn. Other known locations where Edwin spawns are High Pass Hold, Queynos Hills, and Rathe Mountains. After turning in the head say to Kazen Facae, "What about a symbol of the apprentice?" for which you will be given the Symbol of the Apprentice. Then, continue on to the next step.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Twisted Symbol of the Apprentice and Moss</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Venenzi Oberzendi at location -1000, -700 in Nektulos Forest: **Symbol of the Apprentice - Given to you by Kazen Facae for completing the Symbol of the Apprentice Quest. ***Note: Turn in the symbol first and serperatly from the robe. **Flowing Black Robe - Dropped by Najena in Najena (or can be easily bought in the Bazaar). After you turn in the Robe you will be given the Twisted Symbol of the Apprentice and Moss. Then, continue on to the next step.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Symbol of the Serpent</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Emkel Kabae near the stone skeleton tower in Lake Rathetear and then say the following words: **Twisted Symbol of the Apprentice - Given to you by Venenzi Oberzendi for completing the Twisted Symbol of the Apprentice Quest. **Moss - Also given to you by Venenzi Oberzendi for completing the Twisted Symbol of the Apprentice Quest. After turning in the items - say to Emkel Kabae, "The Twisted Symbol of the Apprentice" for which you will be given the Symbol of the Serpent. Then, continue on to the next step.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Scaled Symbol of the Serpent</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Ssessthrass at location 3800, 1600 in the Swamp of No Hope: **Symbol of the Serpent - Given to you by Emkel Kabae for completing the Symbol of the Serpent Quest. ***Note: Ssessthrass is in a house in the pass to go to Field of Bone. After turning in the Symbol you will be given a new Symbol and sent to retrieve manisi herb. You will in return receive the Scaled Symbol of the Serpent. Then, continue on to the next step.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Refined Manisi Herb</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Return to Ssessthrass and turn in the following: **Manisi Herb - Dropped by Grand Herbalist Mak'ha in Chardok ***Note: Grand Herbalist Mak'ha is located in the Herb House in the mines of Chardok. The Herb House is located North of the Chardok Bank, behind a waterfall and small stream. Alternately, it can be reached from the Bridge Keeper or the 'Ledge path' as you descend into the mines. 'A Dizok Herbalist' is the placeholder for the Grand Herbalist, and always spawns in the Herb House, guarded by many Chokidai and Apprentice Herbalists. The Grand Herbalist does not drop the Mansi Herb every time. **Scaled Symbol of the Serpent - Given to you by Ssessthrass for turning in the Symbol of the Serpent. In return yo uwill be given Refined Manisi Herb. Then, continue on to the next step.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Symbol of Testing</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Return to Emkel Kabae in Lake Rathetear and turn in the following: **Refined Manisi Herb - Given to you by Ssessthrass for completing the Refined Manisi Herb Quest. In return you will be given the Symbol of Testing. Then, continue on to the next step.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Symbol of Insanity</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Return to Kazen Facae in Lake Rathetear and give him the Symbol of Testing. Turning in the symbol to Kazen will cause Bone Golem (lvl 55) to spawn close by to the east of Emkel on a little inlet. Kill him. As soon as Bone Golem is killed, the Failed Apprentice (lvl 53) will spawn. Kill him. As soon as the Failed Apprentice is killed, a Tormented Spirit (lvl 55) will spawn. Kill him and loot the Symbol of Insanity. ***Note: All three can be killed with two groups of 50+ with a couple Clerics and Tanks.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Silver Disc</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Acquire the following: **Silver Discs - dropped most commonly by Azeracks on the second isle in the Plane of Sky. ***Note: Azeracks are lvl 53 mobs.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Spiroc Feathers</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Acquire the following: **Spiroc Feathers - dropped by the Watchful Guardians on the 3rd Isle in the Plane of Sky. ***Note: Watchful Guardian are lvl 53-55 mobs.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Black Silk Cape</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Acquire the following: **Black Silk Cape - dropped by the boss of the fourth island, Keeper of Souls, in the Plane of Sky. ***Note: He is a level 60 mob that death touches every 30 seconds. He can quad hit for 400 which is a real nuisance. Also, the cape does not drop every time.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Cloak of Spiroc Feathers</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Jzil Gsix at (loc) in the Plane of Sky quest room: **Silver Disc - dropped by Azeracks on the second isle in the Plane of sky. **Spiroc Feathers - dropped by the Watchful Guardians on the 3rd Isle in the Plane of Sky. **Black Silk Cape - dropped by the boss of the fourth island, Keeper of Souls, in the Plane of Sky. In return, you will be given the Cloak of Spiroc Feathers.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The Eye of Innoruuk</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Acquire the following item: **The Eye of Innoruuk - dropped by Innoruuk himself or the mini-bosses: Maestro of Rancor, a Ashenbone Drake, Magi P' Tasa, and the Master of Spite in the Plane of Hate.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">The Blood of Cazic Thule</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Acquire the following item: **The Blood of Cazic Thule - dropped by the Iron Guardians in front of Cazic’s temple in the Plane of Fear. ***Note: The guardians are level 60 and said to be the second hardest creatures in Plane of Fear.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Drendico Metalbones' Journal</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Drendico Metalbones at 6485, 3829 in Timorous Deep: **Symbol of Insanity - Acquired by completing the Symbol of Insanity Quest. ***Note: Drendico Metalbones is at the docks that take you to the Overthere. If you turn right from the docks and climb onto a stoney hill, you will see this little gnome wandering around. For turning in the Symbol he will give you his journal and asks you to return to him, Eye of Innoruuk, Blood of Cazic-Thule, and Cloak of Spiroc Feathers.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Prepared Reagents Box</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Now, turn in the following components to Drendico Metalbones: **Drendico Metalbones' Journal - given to you by Drendico Metalbones for turning in the Symbol of Insanity **The Eye of Innoruuk - dropped by Innoruk or his mini-bosses. **The Blood of Cazic Thule - dropped by the Iron Guardians. **Cloak of Spiroc Feathers - received for completing the Cloak of Spiroc Feathers Qquest. In return, you will recieve a Prepared Reagents Box.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Complete Epic Quest Phases 1-3</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Prior to starting the final phase of your epic quest, complete Phase 1: Symbol of Insanity Quest; Phase 2: Cloak of Spiroc Feathers; and Phase 3: Prepared Reagents Box.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Tome of Instruction</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Turn in the following to Kazen Facae at location 340, -1600 in Lake Rathetear: **Prepared Reagents Box - given to you by Drendico Metalbones for completing the Prepared Reagents Box Quest. In return, you will be given the Tome of Instruction.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Gkzzallk in a Bottle</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Go to the Plane of Sky and give a Thunder Spirit Princess 10 gold (you will get a message indicating Gkzzallk has spawned). Go to the 3rd isle and give the Tome of Instruction to Gkzzallk and in return he will give you Gkzzallk in a Bottle. ***Note: I have found conflicting information on the amount of money needed to be given to a Thunder Spirit Princess to have Gkzzallk spawn. If the 10 gold doesn't work, try 3 platinum.</td></tr></tbody> </table> <hr id="null" /> <table class="ContentBox" width="100%"> <tbody><tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Epic Reward - Scythe of Shadowed Souls</td></tr> <tr> <td class="ContentBoxBody">Now go back to Kazen Facae and give him the Gkzzallk in a Bottle to receive your Epic: Scythe of Shadowed Souls.</td></tr></tbody> </table> 
							
